	<div id="content-wrap" class="container no-sidebar">
		<div id="primary" class="content-area">
			<main id="main" class="site-main" role="main">

				
					<article id="post-21423" class="post-21423 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-news">

	<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title">Total Hydrogen Solutions Announces Commercial Fueling Agreement with Hyroad Energy to Support Hydrogen Powered Fleets in Texas</h1>
		<div class="entry-meta">
			<span class="byline"> Posted by <span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://pneumaticandhydraulic.com/author/phc/">Pneumatic and Hydraulic Company LLC</a></span></span><span class="posted-on"> on <a href="https://pneumaticandhydraulic.com/news/ths-hyroad-fueling-agreement/" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date published updated" datetime="2026-08-05T13:28:53+00:00">August 5, 2026</time></a></span>		</div><!-- .entry-meta -->

	</header><!-- .entry-header -->
	
	
	<div class="entry-content">
		<div class="wpb-content-wrapper" id="wpb-content-root">
<div id="wpc_6ac065e56130e" class="vc_row wpb_row vc_row-fluid  ">
		<div class="row_inner_wrapper  clearfix">
			<div class="row_inner row_center_content clearfix"><div class="wpb_column vc_column_container vc_col-md-12 vc_col-has-fill"><div class="vc_column-inner vc_custom_1785791745370"><div class="wpb_wrapper">
	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element vc_custom_1785792113385" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<p><span style="color: #000000;"><strong>Katy, TX – August 3, 2026</strong> – Total Hydrogen Solutions (THS), a division of Pneumatic and Hydraulic Company LLC, recently announced a commercial fueling agreement with <a style="color: #000000;" href="https://www.hyroadenergy.com/"><b>Hyroad Energy</b></a> to support the development and operation of a new hydrogen refueling station (HRS) in Katy, Texas. As part of the agreement, Hyroad has committed to the station&#8217;s full fueling capacity through a long-term offtake agreement, providing a reliable hydrogen supply solution for its growing fleet operations across Texas. </span></p>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><span style="color: #000000;">Designed, built, and operated by THS, the hydrogen refueling station features onsite hydrogen production through electrolysis, creating a localized fuel supply which reduces transportation costs and supply chain complexity. The facility is engineered to provide fast-fill fueling capabilities for heavy-duty hydrogen fuel cell trucks and trailers, supporting the increasing demand for zero-emission transportation solutions throughout the region. </span></p>
<p><span style="color: #000000;">The agreement marks a major milestone in the commercialization of hydrogen-powered transportation infrastructure and reflects nearly two years of collaboration between THS and Hyroad Energy. The station is expected to become fully operational later this year. </span></p>
<p><span style="color: #000000;">&#8220;We&#8217;re proud to partner with Hyroad Energy on this important step forward for hydrogen trucking in Texas. This station represents the kind of scalable, reliable infrastructure the industry needs, and it reflects our commitment to delivering end-to-end hydrogen solutions that help fleets transition with confidence,&#8221; said Mark Mire, Owner and CEO of Total Hydrogen Solutions. </span></p>
<p><span style="color: #000000;">The hydrogen refueling station in Katy, TX represents another step in THS&#8217;s strategy to develop scalable hydrogen infrastructure that connects hydrogen production directly to commercial transportation applications. Through turnkey project execution and lifecycle support, THS continues to help customers deploy practical hydrogen solutions that accelerate the transition to lower-emission energy systems. </span></p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element vc_custom_1785792121194" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
			<h3><span style="color: #000000;"><b>About Total Hydrogen Solutions</b></span></h3>
<p><span style="color: #000000;"><span class="TextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0" lang="EN-US" xml:lang="EN-US" data-contrast="auto"><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">Total Hydrogen Solutions (THS) is a comprehensive hydrogen energy systems provider across the full hydrogen lifecycle – from concept and design to installation, </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">maintenance</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0"> and repair. Through its parent company, Pneumatic and Hydraulic Company, </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">LLC, </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">the THS division </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">boasts</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0"> over 65 years of experience in high-pressure systems and fluid power. Supported by a team of engineers, </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">technicians</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0"> and industry experts, THS </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">offers</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0"> extensive inventory of hydrogen products and strong partnerships with leading technology providers to ensure </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">timely</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0"> delivery and innovative solutions. For more information, visit: </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">www.TotalHydrogen.com</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">. For more information about the parent company, visit </span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">www.PneumaticandHydraulic.com</span><span class="NormalTextRun SCXW187112186 BCX0">.</span></span><span class="EOP SCXW187112186 BCX0" data-ccp-props="{}"> </span></span></p>
<h3><span style="color: #000000;"><b>About Hyroad Energy</b> </span></h3>
<p><span style="color: #000000;">Hyroad Energy delivers cutting-edge, zero-emission Class 8 hydrogen fuel cell trucks, designed to meet the needs of fleets while reducing their carbon footprint. Through its innovative pay-per-mile model, Hyroad eliminates the complexity and upfront costs traditionally associated with deploying zero-emission trucks. As a pioneer in hydrogen-powered transportation, Hyroad Energy is leading the charge toward a cleaner, more sustainable future. For more information, visit<a style="color: #000000;" href="http://www.hyroadenergy.com/"> </a><a style="color: #000000;" href="http://www.hyroadenergy.com/">www.hyroadenergy.com</a>  </span></p>

		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="wpb_text_column wpb_content_element vc_custom_1785792127111" >
		<div class="wpb_wrapper">
